    "Are you sure you want to restart the tutorial? Your current progress will be lost." : {

    },
    "At first, no one looked me in the eye. I felt like I’d disappeared after getting my ileostomy. I stopped going out, even to the park. Then one day, I picked up a paintbrush and started painting how I felt—blurry, grey, hidden. But slowly, color returned to my canvas, and to me. A gallery offered to show my art. At the opening, someone said, “Your work made me feel seen.” That’s when I knew: I’m not invisible. I just had to find new ways to be visible." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "At first, no one looked me in the eye. I felt like I’d disappeared after getting my ileostomy. I stopped going out, even to the park. Then one day, I picked up a paintbrush and started painting how I felt—blurry, grey, hidden. But slowly, color returned to my canvas, and to me. A gallery offered to show my art. At the opening, someone said, “Your work made me feel seen.” That’s when I knew: I’m not invisible. I just had to find new ways to be visible."
          }
        },
        "es-419" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Al principio, nadie me miraba a los ojos. Sentí que había desaparecido después de hacerme la ileostomía. Dejé de salir, incluso al parque. Luego, un día, tomé un pincel y empecé a pintar cómo me sentía: borroso, gris, oculto. Pero poco a poco, el color volvió a mi lienzo y a mí. Una galería ofreció mostrar mi arte. En la inauguración, alguien dijo: “Tu obra me hizo sentir visto.” Fue entonces cuando supe: no soy invisible. Solo tuve que encontrar nuevas formas de ser visible."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "All'inizio, nessuno mi guardava negli occhi. Mi sentivo come se fossi scomparsa dopo aver fatto l'ileostomia. Ho smesso di uscire, anche solo per andare al parco. Poi un giorno ho preso un pennello e ho iniziato a dipingere come mi sentivo—sfocata, grigia, nascosta. Ma lentamente, il colore è tornato sulla mia tela, e in me. Una galleria ha voluto esporre le mie opere. All'inaugurazione, qualcuno ha detto: “Il tuo lavoro mi ha fatto sentire visto.” È stato allora che ho capito: non sono invisibile. Dovevo solo trovare nuovi modi per essere visibile."
          }
        }
      }
    },
